    "body": "### Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.\n\nCurrently, fused types need to be declared before they can be used in function signatures. Especially in Python code, declaring fused functions is somewhat ugly and they tend to end up in place in all modules because sharing them is difficult.\n\nHowever, many fused functions (especially internal `cdef` functions) are only used internally inside of the module and could be generated automatically when being called.\n\n### Describe the solution you'd like.\n\nSince Python 3.12, `TypeVar` is implicit, so functions can be declared as simply:\n```python\ndef first_in_list[T](l: list[T]) -> T:\n    return l[0]\n\nfirst_in_list([1,2,3])  # -> 'int'\n```\nhttps://docs.python.org/3.15/library/typing.html#generics\n\nThere is also a way to constrain the allowed types in place:\n```python\ndef first_in_list[T: (str, float)](l: list[T]) -> T:\n    return l[0]\n```\nCython could detect generic functions like this during its analyse declarations phase and create the fused function alternatives at each call site during its type inference and analyse types phases. I expect both phases to be relevant because type inference already needs (or benefits from) the return type.\n\n### Describe alternatives you've considered.\n\n_No response_\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_",
